<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emil von Zelewski</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1854">1854</a>–<a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emil von Zelewski was a German officer who commanded the colonial troops in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a>. In August 1891 he led an expedition against the Hehe chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mkwawa">Mkwawa</a> and was killed with most of his column in an ambush at Lugalo near Iringa, one of the worst defeats suffered by German colonial forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emil-von-zelewski.jpg" alt="Emil von Zelewski" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emil_von_Zelewski.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
